// - Hybrid: +$670.50, 10.56% DD, 71.07% coverage, HC12/15.
// - K1:     -$347.53, 19.74% DD, 70.96% coverage, HC11/15.
// - Human:  +$1,160.99, 2.53% DD, but only 16.86% coverage and HC1/15 — too sparse to be the primary production construction.
// - Stop:   +$117.25, 11.90% DD, 37.59% coverage, HC3/15 — also too sparse/weak.
// Therefore the identity of the preferred broad candidate does NOT change: Hybrid remains ahead of K1 at essentially equal broad
// coverage and materially better net/DD, while Human's surviving subset is not HC-robust. However, previous claims that Hybrid has
// 100% coverage / HC15/15 / ~$1.96k under realistic execution are superseded. The correct new-floor values are 71.07% / HC12/15 /
// +$670.50 / 10.56% DD / 7 positive years.
